  "title": "wsutil: note an optimization done by newer GCC and Clang.",
  "description": "Those compilers recognize the unaligned fetch and store items in a\nspecified byte order \"do it a byte at a time with shifts and masks\"\nidioms and turn them into optimized code, e.g. doing an unaligned load\nand a byte swap if necessary or doing a byte swap if necessary and an\nunaligned store.\n\npragma-onceify the header while we're at it.",
